[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'If you\'ve ever tried to get into local image or&nbsp; video generation, you know just how frustrating&nbsp;&nbsp; the learning process can be. And if you haven\'t&nbsp; explored programs like Comfy UI because you\'re&nbsp;&nbsp; overwhelmed by the complexity of it, this is the&nbsp; video for you. I\'m sure if you have tried Comfy&nbsp;&nbsp; UI before, you\'ve shared an experience that&nbsp; goes something like this. You spend an hour&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'just getting the program launched. You download&nbsp; a workflow, half the nodes are missing, you\'re&nbsp;&nbsp; hunting down custom node packs that won\'t install&nbsp; for whatever reason. Something\'s incompatible with&nbsp;&nbsp; your installed comi version, and 3 hours later,&nbsp; you still haven\'t made a single image or video.&nbsp;&nbsp; I give up. This video is an overview of&nbsp; the best local generation UI out there,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Simply Genen. Simply Genen is basically a desktop&nbsp; app that takes the whole mess and turns it into&nbsp;&nbsp; a super intuitive one-stop UI, and it\'s tailored&nbsp; specifically with AI influencers in mind. Simply&nbsp;&nbsp; Jen just solved all of my headaches, and I can\'t&nbsp; believe more people don\'t know about this yet.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'m going to walk you through the app, show you&nbsp; the character creation and consistency system&nbsp;&nbsp; that they use natively within Simply Genen, how&nbsp; you can build your very own AI influencer, how&nbsp;&nbsp; local versus cloud works, and all of the insane&nbsp; features that have been packed into this awesome&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'program. If you\'re wondering where you can get it,&nbsp; you can grab Simply Genen through the link in the&nbsp;&nbsp; description below. It\'s a onetime purchase, super&nbsp; affordable, there\'s no subscriptions attached,&nbsp;&nbsp; and it\'s updated every week, multiple times a&nbsp; week in some cases, and the installation is pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'straightforward as well. Let\'s look at the layout&nbsp; before we start generating anything. On the left,&nbsp;&nbsp; you\'ve got your main sections. Generate is where&nbsp; you\'ll spend most of your time, and I will be&nbsp;&nbsp; walking you through the simple generation process.&nbsp; And then you have enhance, which covers upscaling&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and post-processing on stuff you\'ve already&nbsp; made. Below that is your library. Characters&nbsp;&nbsp; is where saved faces and personas live. So once&nbsp; you build a consistent character, you can pull it&nbsp;&nbsp; back up instead of starting from scratch. And&nbsp; right below it, products works the same way,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'but for product shots, it\'s useful if you\'re&nbsp; doing a UGC style ad content. Then you\'ve got the&nbsp;&nbsp; studios. UGC Studio and Product Studio are more&nbsp; guided template driven flows for specific types&nbsp;&nbsp; of content, and we\'ll touch on those a bit later.&nbsp; And then under assets, gallery is every image and&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'video you\'ve generated, filterable by model,&nbsp; date, media type, and so on. And below that,&nbsp;&nbsp; the prompt library lets you save and organize&nbsp; prompts you want to reuse. And then finally,&nbsp;&nbsp; we have the marketplace. This is basically just a&nbsp; preset store, even though these are all free and&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'installable locally on your own device. So,&nbsp; this is essentially where you will download&nbsp;&nbsp; every single model that you want to use. And as&nbsp; you can see, they have all different types of&nbsp;&nbsp; models. This is just for image creation. There\'s&nbsp; models like Z image and Z image Turbo, Quen Image,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Crea 2, Flux 2, Hydream, Fire Red, Ernie, Bugu,&nbsp; and so on. At the top of the preset store,&nbsp;&nbsp; you can also filter by video models. And they have&nbsp; all of the most up-to-date local models that you&nbsp;&nbsp; can use such as LTX 2.3 and W 2.2. And there\'s&nbsp; even NSFW options if that is what you are looking&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to generate. Here under the character section,&nbsp; these are all the models that are compatible&nbsp;&nbsp; with the characters that you create natively with&nbsp; inside of Simply Gen. Under the upscale section,&nbsp;&nbsp; there are upscalers like the RTX upscaler and&nbsp; seed VR2. Under the UGC recipes, you can install&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'templates that have your character presenting&nbsp; a certain product or your character using that&nbsp;&nbsp; product. And under the product recipes section,&nbsp; there are templates in which you can advertise&nbsp;&nbsp; and show off your product without a character. So,&nbsp; heading over to the character section, let\'s build&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a character from scratch so you can see the whole&nbsp; process and just how simple it actually is. So,&nbsp;&nbsp; first you\'ll need to click new character and then&nbsp; give it a name, a gender, a bio, and a location.&nbsp;&nbsp; The bio and location are optional and just tagged&nbsp; on as metadata. So, we can skip over this. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'m just going to name this new character Alice.&nbsp; She\'s a woman. And then I\'m going to click next.&nbsp;&nbsp; Now, you can see here we could either upload a&nbsp; picture of Alice if we already have a picture&nbsp;&nbsp; generated or we can generate a base and start&nbsp; from scratch. I\'m going to start from scratch.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, if you\'re generating a base, then you\'ll&nbsp; see here that we have to completely create and&nbsp;&nbsp; customize our character. There are sections such&nbsp; as body type, hair, eyes, skin, and so on. So,&nbsp;&nbsp; I\'m going to go through and create our character.&nbsp; So, you\'ll see as I go through and select all the&nbsp;&nbsp;'

